Real men use their feet.

2526
02:26:02,100 --> 02:26:02,740
Hey, you!

2527
02:26:05,970 --> 02:26:07,350
The hell was that sound?

2528
02:26:07,410 --> 02:26:07,830
You heard that?

2529
02:26:11,900 --> 02:26:12,900
There's an animal here.

2530
02:26:14,340 --> 02:26:14,800
Oh.

2531
02:26:15,360 --> 02:26:16,180
It's a wolf.

2532
02:26:16,420 --> 02:26:17,520
No, it's a...

2533
02:26:17,520 --> 02:26:18,620
Dude, what's the name?

2534
02:26:19,780 --> 02:26:20,240
Fox!

2535
02:26:22,980 --> 02:26:24,800
Even in this game, the foxes sound weird.

2536
02:26:30,920 --> 02:26:31,380
Yeah.

2537
02:26:31,740 --> 02:26:32,880
I'm gonna grab some more of this.

2538
02:26:35,910 --> 02:26:36,930
I'm making jelly.

2539
02:26:40,200 --> 02:26:43,960
And then I will go to the farmer's market.

2540
02:26:44,900 --> 02:26:47,100
Or the state fair.

2541
02:26:48,260 --> 02:26:49,460
There's a name for that in America.

2542
02:26:49,640 --> 02:26:51,240
Where you go and you sell jelly and jam.

2543
02:26:52,280 --> 02:26:54,680
And you bring, like, carnival rides and stuff.

2544
02:26:56,000 --> 02:26:57,320
And there's, like, a petting zoo.

2545
02:26:57,520 --> 02:26:57,720
You know?

2546
02:26:58,880 --> 02:26:59,880
Never been to one of those.

2547
02:27:00,020 --> 02:27:01,360
But I would love to go to one of them.

2548
02:27:05,150 --> 02:27:06,170
More dogs!

2549
02:27:06,310 --> 02:27:07,590
Join my rebellion.

2550
02:27:10,990 --> 02:27:11,970
You're with me.

2551
02:27:13,490 --> 02:27:14,690
A whole army.

2552
02:27:16,590 --> 02:27:17,270
Nice.

2553
02:27:19,670 --> 02:27:22,190
Okay, so we got Audrey and Allie.

2554
02:27:24,030 --> 02:27:25,230
Add them to the mix.

2555
02:27:32,440 --> 02:27:34,120
Oh no, not the water.

2556
02:27:34,960 --> 02:27:37,260
How will we overcome this burden?

2557
02:27:39,320 --> 02:27:41,480
Get ready for quantum teleportation.

2558
02:27:41,640 --> 02:27:42,980
On my mark.

2559
02:27:43,760 --> 02:27:44,400
Three.

2560
02:27:44,760 --> 02:27:45,300
Two.

2561
02:27:45,640 --> 02:27:46,320
One.

2562
02:27:49,060 --> 02:27:49,780
Beautiful!

2563
02:27:50,500 --> 02:27:51,500
Oh shit, come on.

2564
02:27:53,340 --> 02:27:54,240
Let's go.

2565
02:27:58,880 --> 02:27:59,860
Follow me.

2566
02:28:00,820 --> 02:28:03,180
We're going towards the rising sun.

2567
02:28:03,420 --> 02:28:04,760
I mean, the setting sun.

2568
02:28:05,760 --> 02:28:07,580
But it sounded better with rising.

2569
02:28:11,710 --> 02:28:14,970
Audrey, Allie, Billy, Basso, and...

2570
02:28:15,790 --> 02:28:16,510
Bruto!

2571
02:28:19,360 --> 02:28:21,000
Let's see if we can find more dogs on the way.

2572
02:28:21,420 --> 02:28:22,320
That's a big hole.

2573
02:28:24,260 --> 02:28:25,420
Wish I had Elytra.

2574
02:28:25,720 --> 02:28:27,160
I would totally fly through that.

2575
02:28:28,840 --> 02:28:30,620
That seems like a far away dream right now.

2576
02:28:32,780 --> 02:28:33,600
Oh, look at that.

2577
02:28:39,540 --> 02:28:42,380
Look at the way it's setting over the horizon and those trees.

2578
02:28:47,770 --> 02:28:49,230
You got your dogs with you?

2579
02:28:49,230 --> 02:28:51,450
Is there anything else you need in life?

2580
02:28:55,480 --> 02:28:56,460
Dude, that...

2581
02:28:56,460 --> 02:28:57,200
Look at this!

2582
02:28:57,980 --> 02:28:59,040
That is amazing.

2583
02:29:01,830 --> 02:29:02,710
Let's go to bed.

2584
02:29:10,880 --> 02:29:11,400
Ah!

2585
02:29:11,560 --> 02:29:12,160
I fell.

2586
02:29:15,300 --> 02:29:15,800
Um...

2587
02:29:15,800 --> 02:29:16,440
This way.

2588
02:29:18,160 --> 02:29:19,500
And what is that over there?

2589
02:29:21,120 --> 02:29:21,620
Crime!

2590
02:29:21,840 --> 02:29:23,380
You see, I can spot crimes.

2591
02:29:24,300 --> 02:29:25,560
From so far away.

2592
02:29:25,820 --> 02:29:27,220
Even without the glass.

2593
02:29:27,480 --> 02:29:28,240
I saw it.

2594
02:29:28,680 --> 02:29:29,880
That's why I zoomed on it.

2595
02:29:29,940 --> 02:29:31,060
I saw something wasn't right.

2596
02:29:36,240 --> 02:29:36,740
Money!

2597
02:29:39,600 --> 02:29:40,340
You know what?

2598
02:29:40,500 --> 02:29:40,820
Yeah.

2599
02:29:41,020 --> 02:29:41,940
Let's go grab the money.

2600
02:29:44,420 --> 02:29:45,360
I do like that.

2601
02:29:49,160 --> 02:29:50,640
There's also cows we can slay.

2602
02:29:56,210 --> 02:29:57,070
Come on, guys!

2603
02:29:58,750 --> 02:29:59,190
Teleport!

2604
02:30:05,640 --> 02:30:06,220
Everyone's here.

2605
02:30:12,250 --> 02:30:13,390
Alright, you're gonna die.

2606
02:30:14,190 --> 02:30:15,050
Everyone dies.

2607
02:30:16,430 --> 02:30:18,270
I do wonder if I can feed them raw meat.

2608
02:30:18,530 --> 02:30:19,430
Will that make them happy?

2609
02:30:20,950 --> 02:30:22,050
Wait, are they gonna have children?

2610
02:30:26,100 --> 02:30:27,080
Oh my god!

2611
02:30:27,080 --> 02:30:28,100
I never thought about that!

2612
02:30:30,680 --> 02:30:32,080
Of course that would happen!

2613
02:30:38,240 --> 02:30:39,660
They must have adopted, though.

2614
02:30:45,080 --> 02:30:46,120
We gotta cook this meat.

2615
02:30:51,140 --> 02:30:51,860
Wait, wait, wait!

2616
02:30:51,980 --> 02:30:52,760
This is not what I saw.

2617
02:30:54,440 --> 02:30:54,840
Ha!

2618
02:30:54,900 --> 02:30:55,680
That's so much of it!

2619
02:30:55,740 --> 02:30:55,900
Look!

2620
02:30:56,120 --> 02:30:56,820
There's more!

2621
02:30:57,000 --> 02:30:57,560
We're rich!

2622
02:30:58,680 --> 02:30:59,480
Holy cannoli!

2623
02:31:01,660 --> 02:31:03,160
Have you ever seen anything like this?

2624
02:31:07,640 --> 02:31:09,140
We're grabbing this one up here first.

2625
02:31:13,680 --> 02:31:15,400
Dude, I've always wanted to try a cannoli.

2626
02:31:17,020 --> 02:31:17,940
I've never had one.

2627
02:31:18,980 --> 02:31:20,160
I don't even know what's in it.

2628
02:31:20,320 --> 02:31:21,000
Chocolate, I guess.

2629
02:31:28,710 --> 02:31:29,730
I hated that!

2630
02:31:32,310 --> 02:31:32,710
Everyone...

2631
02:31:33,910 --> 02:31:36,710
I guess that answers the old question of...

2632
02:31:37,430 --> 02:31:39,650
Would you follow me into anything blindly?

2633
02:31:40,630 --> 02:31:41,370
And you would.

2634
02:31:46,350 --> 02:31:47,670
Did I see even more money?

2635
02:31:58,770 --> 02:32:00,950
I'm gonna grab the remaining two, and then we're on our way.

2636
02:32:02,750 --> 02:32:03,790
Oh, no, come on.

2637
02:32:08,260 --> 02:32:09,020
Oh, there's more!

2638
02:32:09,600 --> 02:32:10,520
How did I miss that one?

2639
02:32:13,560 --> 02:32:15,280
Yo, why is there so much money here?

2640
02:32:17,760 --> 02:32:18,920
Did that give a lot of experience?

2641
02:32:29,530 --> 02:32:30,790
Okay, so I think it's...

2642
02:32:31,650 --> 02:32:32,290
Right here.

2643
02:32:32,530 --> 02:32:32,670
Yeah.

2644
02:32:34,790 --> 02:32:35,390
What is that?

2645
02:32:36,910 --> 02:32:38,050
It's a frog!

2646
02:32:38,050 --> 02:32:38,210
Frog!

2647
02:32:39,570 --> 02:32:40,050
Hmm.

2648
02:32:43,160 --> 02:32:47,920
I never did figure out what frogs eat, so I never could replicate them in the lab.

2649
02:32:49,520 --> 02:32:53,780
Maybe, uh, this time around, I'll manage to find out.

2650
02:33:00,740 --> 02:33:02,280
This gravel is annoying.

2651
02:33:07,860 --> 02:33:08,900
God, that's annoying.

2652
02:33:09,140 --> 02:33:10,380
I just want to scream.

2653
02:33:18,040 --> 02:33:22,060
By the way, doggos, some of you are expected to die on this trip.

2654
02:33:22,640 --> 02:33:24,280
Not everyone will survive it.

2655
02:33:26,380 --> 02:33:26,780
Swamp!

2656
02:33:29,180 --> 02:33:29,580
Wonderful!

2657
02:33:31,260 --> 02:33:32,520
Let's see what we can find here.

2658
02:33:37,180 --> 02:33:38,620
God, I need to...

2659
02:33:38,620 --> 02:33:38,880
Oh.

2660
02:33:39,560 --> 02:33:40,320
Oh, man.

2661
02:33:41,100 --> 02:33:42,760
Okay, who cares about fire charges?

2662
02:33:42,780 --> 02:33:43,240
Not me.

2663
02:33:45,280 --> 02:33:46,700
I don't care about these sticks either.

2664
02:33:46,900 --> 02:33:47,500
Or, you know what?

2665
02:33:47,700 --> 02:33:48,920
I don't care about the fire resistance.

2666
02:33:49,080 --> 02:33:49,380
I said it.

2667
02:33:49,620 --> 02:33:50,200
Both of them, gone.

2668
02:33:50,460 --> 02:33:50,620
Yep.

2669
02:33:51,460 --> 02:33:52,080
Off my hands.

2670
02:33:54,240 --> 02:33:55,820
And we're also going to throw away...

2671
02:33:55,820 --> 02:33:56,460
We don't need these keys!

2672
02:33:57,220 --> 02:33:57,540
Gone!

2673
02:33:58,800 --> 02:33:59,780
That was so brave of me.

2674
02:34:02,080 --> 02:34:03,080
I can't believe I did that.

2675
02:34:04,000 --> 02:34:04,640
A portal!

2676
02:34:06,840 --> 02:34:07,460
We shall...

2677
02:34:07,460 --> 02:34:08,760
We shall go have a gander at that.

2678
02:34:09,620 --> 02:34:10,560
I kind of want these.

2679
02:34:17,090 --> 02:34:18,250
We're going to put them on the lake.

2680
02:34:18,370 --> 02:34:20,610
We're going to make the lake next to our house, like...

2681
02:34:20,610 --> 02:34:21,830
Really nice.

2682
02:34:22,150 --> 02:34:24,410
Green and clean and...

2683
02:34:24,410 --> 02:34:25,750
You know, really...

2684
02:34:25,750 --> 02:34:26,650
Filled with life.

2685
02:34:28,130 --> 02:34:29,650
And then we're going to pollute it.

2686
02:34:30,410 --> 02:34:32,890
With pipes of industry.

2687
02:34:35,390 --> 02:34:36,930
That's the look I'm going for.

2688
02:34:42,140 --> 02:34:42,480
Jump!

2689
02:34:42,820 --> 02:34:43,060
Jump!

2690
02:34:49,960 --> 02:34:52,140
A golden apple, you say?

2691
02:34:54,180 --> 02:34:55,180
Why not?

2692
02:34:56,240 --> 02:34:58,120
Don't really want anything else.

2693
02:34:59,560 --> 02:35:00,940
I just don't have room for it.

2694
02:35:01,940 --> 02:35:04,800
And I don't have enough obsidian to make that portal.

2695
02:35:06,000 --> 02:35:06,720
I say no.

2696
02:35:12,610 --> 02:35:14,370
I think I'm actually close to home.

2697
02:35:18,740 --> 02:35:19,920
Wait, I better be close to home.

2698
02:35:22,200 --> 02:35:25,120
I have, like, approximately two minutes left.

2699
02:35:26,120 --> 02:35:26,880
To find home.

2700
02:35:27,140 --> 02:35:27,540
Oh, shit.

2701
02:35:27,680 --> 02:35:28,080
Oh, shit.

2702
02:35:28,180 --> 02:35:28,620
We gotta go!

2703
02:35:31,240 --> 02:35:31,920
There's no way!

2704
02:35:46,580 --> 02:35:47,420
Come on, doggos!

2705
02:35:47,800 --> 02:35:48,960
Follow me on the lilypads!

2706
02:35:52,150 --> 02:35:52,630
Oh, shit!

2707
02:35:52,670 --> 02:35:53,210
You're not doing it!

2708
02:35:55,330 --> 02:35:55,810
Oh, no.

2709
02:35:55,870 --> 02:35:56,570
We're not going to make it!

2710
02:35:58,990 --> 02:35:59,530
I can't.

2711
02:35:59,590 --> 02:35:59,910
I can't.

2712
02:36:00,070 --> 02:36:00,670
It's too deep.

2713
02:36:00,970 --> 02:36:01,450
I'm coming back.

2714
02:36:03,290 --> 02:36:04,810
Wait, they're somehow making it.

2715
02:36:04,850 --> 02:36:04,970
Look!

2716
02:36:07,770 --> 02:36:08,310
Oh, no.

2717
02:36:08,390 --> 02:36:09,030
Not the lightning.

2718
02:36:12,480 --> 02:36:13,300
This is not good.

2719
02:36:15,940 --> 02:36:16,740
Follow me.

2720
02:36:17,000 --> 02:36:19,340
I know a safe path through these wastes.

2721
02:36:23,110 --> 02:36:24,430
Whatever you do...

2722
02:36:24,430 --> 02:36:27,470
Billy, Basso, Bruno, Audrey, and Allie...

2723
02:36:28,610 --> 02:36:30,210
Do not follow the lights.

2724
02:36:33,360 --> 02:36:33,920
Okay?

2725
02:36:40,040 --> 02:36:40,980
We got incoming!

2726
02:36:41,940 --> 02:36:43,000
Bruno, you take left!

2727
02:36:43,180 --> 02:36:43,440
Billy!

2728
02:36:45,500 --> 02:36:46,360
That's it, Audrey.

2729
02:36:47,540 --> 02:36:48,500
We got this.

2730
02:36:49,740 --> 02:36:50,300
Teamwork.

2731
02:36:51,860 --> 02:36:52,800
Good job, good job.

2732
02:36:55,770 --> 02:36:56,410
Creeper on the right.

2733
02:36:56,510 --> 02:36:57,150
We don't deal with that.

2734
02:36:58,910 --> 02:36:59,570
We run.

2735
02:37:01,210 --> 02:37:02,930
What the fuck is going on here?

2736
02:37:05,570 --> 02:37:06,690
There's explosions everywhere.

2737
02:37:06,850 --> 02:37:07,630
It's like a war zone.

2738
02:37:14,470 --> 02:37:15,470
We may have to go to bed.

2739
02:37:19,070 --> 02:37:19,450
Sleep.

2740
02:37:22,130 --> 02:37:23,110
Right underneath the tree.

2741
02:37:25,170 --> 02:37:25,550
Quick!

2742
02:37:25,710 --> 02:37:26,130
Spider coming!

2743
02:37:27,870 --> 02:37:28,970
Protect me while I sleep.

2744
02:37:29,610 --> 02:37:30,610
I wonder if they do that.

2745
02:37:36,500 --> 02:37:37,280
There we go.

2746
02:37:37,640 --> 02:37:38,160
No problem.

2747
02:37:40,780 --> 02:37:43,420
Unfortunately, I didn't make it in 30 minutes.

2748
02:37:45,560 --> 02:37:46,500
It is what it is.

2749
02:37:46,660 --> 02:37:48,740
I overestimated my abilities.

2750
02:37:49,860 --> 02:37:54,480
My navigational skills are just not what they once were, you know?

2751
02:37:55,700 --> 02:37:58,620
Hey, we finally made it to the crimes, as much as we saw in the distance.

2752
02:38:12,660 --> 02:38:13,800
That's kind of nice looking.

2753
02:38:15,260 --> 02:38:15,720
Ew!

2754
02:38:16,660 --> 02:38:18,880
Dude, we got Beauty and the Beast here.

2755
02:38:18,900 --> 02:38:19,560
Look at that!

2756
02:38:27,830 --> 02:38:29,030
Let me see this compass.

2757
02:38:34,990 --> 02:38:40,650
I also got to start worrying about whether or not I'm overshooting my home.

2758
02:38:42,270 --> 02:38:42,790
You know?

2759
02:38:43,710 --> 02:38:45,250
Because that could really be a thing.

2760
02:39:01,710 --> 02:39:04,530
The fact that we're seeing this wood right here is a good indicator.

2761
02:39:10,050 --> 02:39:12,430
But at this point, I don't really know how far away I am.

2762
02:39:14,650 --> 02:39:17,150
I feel like I should be close, because I've been wandering for ages.

2763
02:39:24,390 --> 02:39:25,410
Give me your meat.

2764
02:39:30,050 --> 02:39:32,930
I think I actually did bring my crank, and then I left it somewhere.

2765
02:39:33,930 --> 02:39:37,090
Because I wouldn't just have a saw in my inventory and not a crank, right?

2766
02:39:38,490 --> 02:39:39,570
That doesn't seem right.

2767
02:39:48,620 --> 02:39:51,000
Wait, didn't I spawn in a swamp?

2768
02:39:54,440 --> 02:39:55,300
This could be it.

2769
02:40:04,150 --> 02:40:05,550
This may be the swamp.

2770
02:40:07,110 --> 02:40:09,070
Which means we are indeed coming from the east.

2771
02:40:10,470 --> 02:40:11,350
Which ain't good.

2772
02:40:12,870 --> 02:40:13,850
Actually, it is okay.

2773
02:40:14,050 --> 02:40:16,230
Because that means we're just going to go west, and we should be fine.

2774
02:40:24,970 --> 02:40:25,770
Sup, Fragos.

2775
02:40:35,300 --> 02:40:36,920
Dude, that's a huge mushroom!

2776
02:40:37,040 --> 02:40:37,540
Look at this one!

2777
02:40:39,920 --> 02:40:41,340
Have you ever seen one this big?

2778
02:40:44,120 --> 02:40:44,520
Damn!

2779
02:40:45,260 --> 02:40:46,420
Why is that one so big?

2780
02:40:52,570 --> 02:40:54,430
Yeah, this is like the max size I've ever seen.

2781
02:40:59,320 --> 02:40:59,980
Oh wait, jungle?

2782
02:41:00,100 --> 02:41:00,820
I don't know that!

2783
02:41:03,240 --> 02:41:03,900
I'm lost.

2784
02:41:08,760 --> 02:41:09,500
Oh no.

2785
02:41:11,520 --> 02:41:12,940
There shouldn't be any jungle here.

2786
02:41:33,310 --> 02:41:35,350
Wait, the compass is kind of reacting a little?

2787
02:41:35,350 --> 02:41:36,450
I need to just go on a straight...

2788
02:41:36,450 --> 02:41:38,050
Yeah, yeah, okay, we're actually kind of close.

2789
02:41:39,850 --> 02:41:44,890
The fact that the compass is twitching when I run in a straight line means we're actually close.

2790
02:41:51,290 --> 02:41:53,070
At least close to where I spawned.

2791
02:41:54,930 --> 02:42:02,630
But let's not forget, I did wander off for quite a while before I did find the place I decided to settle my land on.

2792
02:42:02,630 --> 02:42:03,430
Wait, this is it!

2793
02:42:03,750 --> 02:42:04,830
This is where I spawned!

2794
02:42:05,970 --> 02:42:08,290
It's like the weird Swamp 2.0.

2795
02:42:09,930 --> 02:42:10,930
Yeah, yeah, the penis!

2796
02:42:11,150 --> 02:42:11,430
Remember?

2797
02:42:12,970 --> 02:42:14,210
That's how we started this thing.

2798
02:42:17,510 --> 02:42:21,010
So, yeah, I still don't understand how we're coming from the east, but...

2799
02:42:21,830 --> 02:42:23,030
Usually I come from the west.

